       "The Trail of Tears (1838–39): the Cherokee were forced to march hundreds of miles on foot; thousands died.",
       "The California Gold Rush of 1849 further accelerated the displacement of native peoples.",
       "Surviving natives were confined to limited areas called \"reservations\".",
       "At the Battle of Little Bighorn (1876) natives won a victory, but resistance was crushed at the Wounded Knee massacre (1890).",
       "In Australia, Aboriginal peoples had lived for more than 40,000 years.",
       "Captain Cook claimed the east coast for Britain in 1770; a penal colony was founded at Sydney in 1788.",
       "The doctrine of \"terra nullius\" (land belonging to no one) denied Aboriginal land rights.",
       "In the frontier wars Aboriginal people resisted, but lost their lands and hunting grounds.",
       "In the 20th century, assimilation policies were enforced — under the \"Stolen Generations\", children were taken from their families.",
